From e58895ebf64271e2b64bf09c076fed4ba73e5ec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zortos <zortosdev@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:37:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] host1x/vp9: propagate range encoder carries in the
 buffer (#2070)

A carry in VpxRangeEncoder::Write walked back through Common::Stream.
Stream::Seek ignores the offset while the position is at the end, so
PeekByte read past the buffer and threw std::out_of_range, which killed
the CDmaPusher thread (FF Resonance cutscene, #1896). Carry into the
written bytes as libvpx's vpx_write does.

Co-authored-by: capy-ai[bot] <230910855+capy-ai[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 833fdf671d8ca27601b950f6a564000e65c64e28)
